          "confidence": "stated",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake",
            "claim": "c037"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-038",
          "text": "Deploy the application to Google Cloud Run.",
          "category": "ops",
          "confidence": "stated",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake",
            "claim": "c038"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-039",
          "text": "Authenticate every user with a persistent named identity and session, since named human decisions and role separation are required.",
          "category": "security",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-040",
          "text": "Model a central Deal entity holding borrower details, requested/exposure amount, current stage, status, assigned owner, and created/updated timestamps; all workflow artifacts hang off it.",
          "category": "data",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-041",
          "text": "Support uploading and storing borrower documents against a deal, with document type, checksum, and upload metadata, so the document extraction stage and citations have a durable target.",
          "category": "data",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-042",
          "text": "Define the standard spread template as a versioned structured schema of named line items (periods, values, units), not free text, so ratios can be computed deterministically from it.",
          "category": "data",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-043",
          "text": "Store citations as structured references (document id plus page/section/cell locator, or ratio/policy-rule id) rather than prose, so every cited number and memo assertion is machine-verifiable and clickable.",
          "category": "data",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-044",
          "text": "Store lending policy as configurable rule data (concentration limits, prohibited industry list, LTV caps) seeded with a documented default ruleset, and version it so audit entries reference the policy version applied.",
          "category": "data",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-045",
          "text": "Encode the risk grading rubric as versioned configuration with documented default bands, and display the rubric and the specific band hit alongside each assigned grade so the grade is explainable.",
          "category": "functional",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-046",
          "text": "Enforce workflow progression with an explicit server-side state machine that rejects illegal or out-of-order stage transitions.",
          "category": "functional",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-047",
          "text": "Support a credit officer 'return' action that sends a deal back to an earlier stage with a required written reason and reassigns it to the analyst queue.",
          "category": "functional",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-048",
          "text": "Provide analyst work queues with assignment and claim semantics, since the triage agent routes requests to analyst queues.",
          "category": "functional",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-049",
          "text": "Provide a human review UI for each agent output showing the draft alongside its citations, with accept, edit, and reject actions; the acceptance records the reviewing user and any edits.",
          "category": "ux",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-050",
          "text": "Implement the audit trail as append-only storage with no update or delete path exposed at the application or API layer, each entry carrying actor, action, timestamp, and before/after payload.",
          "category": "data",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-051",
          "text": "Expose a per-deal audit timeline view so reviewers and auditors can read the full history of state changes, calculations, agent drafts, and human decisions in order.",
          "category": "ux",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-052",
          "text": "Model policy exceptions as first-class records with rule reference, written rationale, status, and resolver identity; an open exception blocks approval until explicitly waived or resolved by an authorized human.",
          "category": "functional",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-053",
          "text": "Enforce RBAC server-side on every endpoint and enforce row-level scoping so a relationship manager cannot read another RM's deals via API or direct object reference.",
          "category": "security",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-054",
          "text": "Scope Portfolio Q&A retrieval to the asking user's RBAC permissions so the agent cannot leak deal data the user is not entitled to see.",
          "category": "security",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-055",
          "text": "Give each agent an explicit allowlist of read/write tools that excludes any approval, decline, stage-advance, ratio-write, or grade-write capability, so the no-agent-decision rule holds structurally.",
          "category": "agent",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-056",
          "text": "Record every agent invocation with agent id, model, prompt version, inputs, outputs, token usage, latency, and outcome, to support evals and audit reconstruction.",
          "category": "ops",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-057",
          "text": "Compute SLA idle time using a business-day calendar that excludes weekends and configurable bank holidays, measured from the last meaningful activity on the deal.",
          "category": "functional",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-058",
          "text": "Provide deal list, search, and filter capability (by stage, owner, risk grade, exposure, age) with the pipeline board grouped by workflow stage.",
          "category": "ux",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-059",
          "text": "Protect borrower financial data with encryption in transit and at rest, secrets held in a managed secret store, and no financial figures or PII written to application logs.",
          "category": "security",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-060",
          "text": "Provide Cloud Run operational readiness: containerized build, health/readiness endpoints, structured JSON logging, configuration via environment, and stateless request handling.",
          "category": "ops",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-061",
          "text": "Isolate all deterministic ratio and grading logic in a pure, side-effect-free module with fixed rounding and divide-by-zero rules, so it is directly unit-testable and reusable.",
          "category": "functional",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-062",
          "text": "Guard approval and stage-transition endpoints against concurrent or duplicate submission so a deal cannot be double-approved or advanced twice.",
          "category": "functional",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-063",
          "text": "Capture the adverse-action reason as a selection from a controlled reason-code list plus required free-text detail, so declines are consistently documented and reportable.",
          "category": "functional",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-064",
          "text": "Handle agent failure, timeout, or low-confidence output by leaving the stage un-advanced and surfacing a retry or manual-completion path to the assigned human, never by auto-advancing.",
          "category": "ops",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-065",
          "text": "Ship seed data covering all three roles and a representative deal in each workflow stage so the pipeline board, SLA dashboard, and approval tiers are demonstrable end to end.",
          "category": "ops",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-066",
          "text": "Deliver the product as a web application usable on standard desktop browsers, since relationship managers, analysts, and officers each work in distinct in-app views.",
          "category": "ux",
          "confidence": "inferred",
          "provenance": {
            "source": "src_intake"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "R-067",
          "text": "Identity source for authentication is unspecified: whether the system integrates with the bank's existing SSO/OIDC identity provider (roles supplied as external claims) or owns local user accounts and role assignment itself.",
          "category": "security",
          "confidence": "unknown"
        },
        {
          "id": "R-068",
          "text": "Credit committee approval mechanics above $1M are unspecified: whether approval is a single action by any committee member, or a multi-member vote requiring a defined quorum/threshold recorded per voter.",
          "category": "functional",
          "confidence": "unknown"
        },
        {
          "id": "R-069",
          "text": "The basis of 'exposure amount' for approval tiering is unspecified: whether it is the requested amount of the single deal, or aggregate outstanding plus proposed exposure across the borrower and its related entities.",
          "category": "functional",
